Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:01.310
Welcome to the course.

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:03.220
I'm Lauren,
I'm a course developer here at Udacity,

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:05.630
and I have a background in
experimental psychology.

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:07.810
&gt;&gt; And I'm Roni,
I'm the program manager at Google.

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:10.340
I run a global program called
Launch Bed to help startups launch

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:11.610
high quality apps.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.420
My background is in startup marketing,
and

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:16.780
I love mentoring startups on how
to think marketing from day one.

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:18.950
And this is what they're going
to learn in this course.

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:21.190
Marketing helps you
understand your user,

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:24.110
focus your product on your user needs,
and take your product to market.

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:27.020
&gt;&gt; But this isn't going to
be a marketing 101 class.

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:29.550
This is more of an applied
marketing course.

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:32.980
&gt;&gt; Yeah, we set up this course to mimic
what you would go through when creating,

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:36.210
launching it,
iterating on your own marketing plan.

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:39.090
The lessons in this course
are divided into several stages.

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:43.540
Like the understanding stage,
the prepare stage, launch, iterate,

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:44.230
and scale.

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:45.470
So tell us more about that.

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:47.840
&gt;&gt; We'll start by understanding
the market we play in, or

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:51.290
the users, how we're going to segment
them, how we're going to position our

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:54.270
product in one competition and
what's our value position?

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:56.515
Then, we'll prepare everything
that is worth the launch.

00:00:56.515 --> 00:00:59.590
&gt;From the marketing plan, all the way to
the landing pages, and cover the launch

00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:03.220
itself, including PR and how to grow
your user base, from one to 1,000.

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:06.420
Then we'll learn how to scale,
with paid advertising and

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:07.880
free growth hacking tips.

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:11.230
And finally, how to iterate and
keep improving you product in marketing

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:13.770
based on your measurements and
analytics.

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:16.770
But marketing's so much more than
just advertising and social media.

00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:19.060
It's about truly
understanding the market,

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:22.100
how to best build your product and
how to understand your customers and

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:25.100
their needs and
where you fit with the industry.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.730
&gt;&gt; In this first lesson we'll cover
market segmentation, competition, and

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:30.055
value proposition.

00:01:30.055 --> 00:01:33.480
By the end of this lesson, you'll have
a better understanding of your users and

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:36.860
where you fit in the market, based on
things like your variable position and

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:38.410
competitive analysis.

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:40.840
&gt;&gt; So let's sign into
the understanding part of marketing.

